{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>Then the king promoted</b> — רבי [he promoted]. Some say: מדינה [medina] means province. If so, how did Ahasuerus have 127 מדינה, and a king who has ten is a great king? And it is written [concerning] וגזל ומשפט וצדק — look at מדינה, whose meaning is the royal city. And it is written: וליהוד שכינתא לבית אלהא רבא [and to the Jew, [news] reached the house of the great El]. And further: ואני בשושן הבירה אשר בעילם המדינה [and I, in Shushan the capital, which is in Elam the medina]. And if עילם is a province, why did he not say במדינת עילם [in the medina of Elam], as they explained regarding מדינת בבל [the medina of Babylon]?!" "<b>and chief officer</b> — like: ויבא סגנים [and officers came]."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The Aramaic phrase וגזל ומשפט וצדק appears corrupt or out of context here; translated hyper-literally as written. The Aramaic citation וליהוד שכינתא varies from the Masoretic text of Daniel 2:5 (ליהוד שכינתא לבית אלהא רבא); translated as found in the commentary."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:29.717002202Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}